@@ -67,6 +67,42 @@ MinIO in-cluster:
 ### Runtime artifact fetch/verify (initContainer)
 Deployments now include an initContainer that:
 1) downloads the artifact from S3/MinIO
 2) verifies sha256 and signature
 3) extracts/copies into `/models` (emptyDir shared with Triton/vLLM)
 
-For MinIO, ensure the serving namespace has credentials available (IRSA/instance role for AWS, or MinIO access keys).
+For AWS S3 on EKS:
+- Prefer IRSA so pods do not need static credentials.
+
+For MinIO:
+- Set these env vars on the Aegis API (temporary/self-contained option):
+  - `AEGIS_MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=...`
+  - `AEGIS_MINIO_SECRET_KEY=...`
+  The deployer will create a tenant-namespace secret `aegis-s3-creds` and attach it to initContainers.
+
+Production recommendation:
+- Replace this with External Secrets Operator or Vault Agent injector.
+
+### Vault auth (self-contained vs production)
+Self-contained (NOT recommended long term):
+- Set `AEGIS_VAULT_TOKEN=...` on the Aegis API
+  - deployer will create secret `aegis-vault-token` in each tenant namespace
+
+Production recommendation:
+- Use Vault Kubernetes auth + Vault Agent injector to provide a short-lived token to the initContainer,
+  or use External Secrets to sync Vault token/approles into namespace.
 
 ## Kubernetes config
 - `AEGIS_K8S_CONFIG=auto|incluster|kubeconfig`
